# Testing rule

Full guidance: `docs/framework/07-unit-testing.md`.

## Derive from acceptance criteria

- Start from `prd.md` §11 (ACs) and `technical-plan.md` §7 (test strategy),
  not from the implementation. Expected values come from the AC text.
- Test names carry the AC ID: `test_ac3_rejects_more_than_10000_rows`,
  `it("AC-3: rejects more than 10,000 rows")`.
- After adding tests, update `test-plan.md` §1 so every AC has a row.

## Structure

- Arrange / Act / Assert; one behaviour per test.
- Cover unhappy paths for each unit: empty input, boundaries, invalid input,
  downstream failure, permission denied, duplicate submission.
- At least one test per external dependency simulating its failure.

## Determinism and speed

- No real clock, network, randomness, or filesystem without an injected fake.
- Unit suite should run in under a minute; move slow tests to
  `tests/integration/`.
- Never "fix" a flaky test by retrying; fix or delete it.

## Assumptions

- If you are unsure of an expected value, do not invent it. Add an
  `OQ-n` (Assumption) to `open-questions.md` and mark the test
  `skip` with the `OQ` reference until it is Accepted.
- Skipped / xfail tests must reference an `OQ-n` or issue.

## Fixtures

- Fixture files start with a short comment: what scenario they represent
  and where the data came from. List them in `test-plan.md` §4.
